\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\cf1\b\f0\fs32{APP_NAME} v{APP_VERSION}\cf2\b0\fs20\par  
\par
\cf1\b\fs24 Introduction\cf2\b0\fs20\par
Welcome to the {APP_NAME} program! This tool is designed to streamline and automate the process of generating, processing, and distributing various quote conversion reports. It aims to reduce manual effort, improve consistency, and provide timely information.\par
The program offers both manual control via a user interface and powerful automated capabilities for scheduled report generation.\par
\par
\cf1\b\fs24 How the Application Works (Overview)\cf2\b0\fs20\par
The application orchestrates several components:\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 User Interface (UI):\b0  Allows for manual selection of report types, date ranges, and processing options. It also provides access to configuration settings and logs.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Crystal Report Wrapper:\b0  An external service used to extract raw report data from the primary business system (via Crystal Reports).\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Excel Processing:\b0  Utilises templates to process the raw data into final, formatted Excel reports. This includes data cleaning, calculations, and potentially filtering.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Email Distribution:\b0  Sends the final reports to configured recipients via SMTP.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Automation Engine:\b0  Handles scheduled, automated generation and emailing of predefined reports based on configuration.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Configuration Files:\b0  Uses \cf3 `appsettings.json`\cf2  for main application default settings (like SMTP, paths, auto-run hour, daily run status, logging parameters, operational settings) and a separate \cf3 `autoReportDefinitions.json`\cf2  (in the same folder) to store the list of all automated report configurations. User-specific JSON files (in your AppData folder) are used for customisations like email recipients, greetings, and bank holidays.\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\cf1\b\fs24 How to Use the Application (Manual Operation)\cf2\b0\fs20\par
\cf4\b\fs22 Main Interface Elements:\cf2\b0\fs20\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Report Type:\cf2\b0  Dropdown to select the desired report period (e.g., Daily, Weekly).\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 From / To Dates:\cf2\b0  Date pickers for defining the report range. These are often auto-filled based on the Report Type.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Financial Year:\cf2\b0  Dropdown (visible for certain report types like Weekly or Custom) to specify the financial year context.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Report Settings Group:\cf2\b0\par

\pard\fi-720\li1080       \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Send to only Femi?:\cf2\b0  (Visible for non-Daily, non-Custom manual reports) Restricts email distribution.\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Skip Sending Email:\cf2\b0  If ticked, the program will generate and process the report files locally but will not send an email.\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Action Buttons:\cf2\b0  Used to generate and process reports. Appearance depends on '1-Click Processing' mode (see Options Menu).\par

\pard\fi-720\li1080       \f1\'b7\tab\i\f0 Standard Mode (2-button):\i0  \cf5\b Create Report\cf2\b0  then \cf5\b Process & Email Report\cf2\b0 .\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\i\f0 1-Click Mode:\i0  A single \cf5\b Generate, Process & Email Report\cf2\b0  button.\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 View Buttons:\cf2\b0  Appear after successful generation: \cf5\b View Raw Report\cf2\b0  and \cf5\b View Processed Analysis\cf2\b0 .\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Enable/Disable Daily Auto Run @ \{AUTO_RUN_HOUR\}:\cf2\b0  Toggles the automated daily report generation feature.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Status Bar:\cf2\b0  Displays the current status of operations (left) and auto-run status (right).\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\cf4\b\fs22 Step-by-Step Guide for Manual Report Generation:\cf2\b0\fs20\par
\b 1. Select Report Type:\b0\par
Choose from the \cf5\b Report Type\cf2\b0  dropdown. Dates will often adjust automatically. Bank holidays (England & Wales, plus custom) are considered for 'previous working day' calculations.\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Daily:\cf2\b0  Report for the \i previous working day\i0 .\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Daily (5days >= \'a31000):\cf2\b0  Covers the \i previous five working days\i0 . After raw data generation, it filters for estimates with a 'Net Value' of \'a31000 or more before final analysis.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Weekly:\cf2\b0  Covers a \i 15-day rolling period ending on the current day\i0 . Data is appended to a central Excel file used by Power BI.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Monthly:\cf2\b0  Report for the \i previous full calendar month\i0 .\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Quarterly:\cf2\b0  Report for the \i previous full calendar quarter\i0 .\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Annual:\cf2\b0  Report for the \i previous full financial year ({FINANCIAL_YEAR_START_INFO} - 30/4 or next day)\i0 .\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Custom:\cf2\b0  Allows manual selection of 'From' and 'To' dates. If you change dates for any other report type, it will automatically switch to 111'Custom'.\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\b 2. Adjust Dates (Optional):\b0\par
If 'Custom' is selected, or if you wish to override the auto-calculated dates for other types, use the \cf5\b From Date\cf2\b0  and \cf5\b To Date\cf2\b0  pickers. Changing dates will set the Report Type to 'Custom'.\par

\b 3. Select Financial Year (If Applicable):\b0\par
For 'Weekly' or 'Custom' reports, the \cf5\b Financial Year\cf2\b0  dropdown may be visible. Select the appropriate financial year if the report data needs to be associated with a specific year for Power BI updates or analysis.\par

\b 4. Configure Report Settings:\b0\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\f0 Tick \cf5\b Send to only Femi?:\cf2\b0  if you want to restrict the email distribution to a predefined IT/admin list. This is typically used for testing or specific non-standard reports.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\f0 Tick \cf5\b Skip Sending Email\cf2\b0  if you only want to generate the report files locally and do not wish for an email to be sent.

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\b 5. Process the Report:\b0\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\f0 If using \i Standard Mode\i0 , first click \cf5\b Create Report\cf2\b0 . Wait for the status to indicate completion. Then, click \cf5\b Process & Email Report\cf2\b0 .\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\f0 If using \i 1-Click Mode\i0  (see Options Menu to enable), click the single \cf5\b Generate, Process & Email Report\cf2\b0  button.

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\b 6. Manual Excel Refresh (for Monthly, Quarterly, Annual, Custom reports):\b0\par
For these report types, the Excel template contains PivotTables that require manual refreshing after the data is populated. You will be prompted:\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\f0 The Excel file will open automatically.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\f0 If prompted by Excel, click \b 'Enable Editing'\b0 .\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\f0 Specifically, ensure PivotTables on the 'OrderPivot' and 'Estimate Success PivotTable' sheets are updated. You may need to right-click them and select 'Refresh'. Check any Slicers as well.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 SAVE\b0  the Excel file.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 CLOSE\b0  Excel.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\f0 The application will then ask you to confirm if you want to proceed with emailing the (now refreshed) report.

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\b 7. Viewing Reports:\b0\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\f0 After the raw report is generated, the \cf5\b View Raw Report\cf2\b0  button becomes active. Click it to open the raw Excel data file.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\f0 After the report is processed (and emailed, if not skipped), the \cf5\b View Processed Analysis\cf2\b0  button becomes active. Click it to open the final, formatted Excel report.\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\cf1\b\fs24 Options & Settings Menus Explained\cf2\b0\fs20\par
The menus provide access to various settings and tools:\par
\b Main Menu:\b0\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Options\cf2\b0  (Sub-menu):\par

\pard\fi-720\li1080       \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Enable 1-Click Processing:\cf2\b0  Toggles between two-button and single-button processing mode.\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Set Auto-Run Hour...:\cf2\b0  Change the hour (0-23) for the daily auto-run check. Current: \b{AUTO_RUN_HOUR}\b0 .\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Manage Automated Reports...:\cf2\b0  Manage all automated report definitions (add, edit, delete, enable/disable).\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Dark Mode:\cf2\b0  Toggles the application's visual theme.\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 View Configuration:\cf2\b0  Displays critical file paths and settings from `appsettings.json`.\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Validate Configuration:\cf2\b0  Quick check of essential configurations.\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Manage Custom Bank Holidays:\cf2\b0  Add/remove custom bank holidays.\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Manage Email Recipients:\cf2\b0  Customise *user-specific overrides* for email lists.\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Manage Email Greetings:\cf2\b0  Customise *user-specific overrides* for email greetings.\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Open Logs Folder:\cf2\b0  Opens the directory with detailed log files.\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Open Auto Report Definitions File:\cf2\b0  Opens the \cf3 `autoReportDefinitions.json`\cf2  file for viewing.\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Edit appsettings.json:\cf2\b0  Opens the main configuration file (`appsettings.json`) for advanced settings. \cf6\i Use with caution!\cf2\i0\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Exit:\cf2\b0  Closes the application.\par
	  \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Settings...:\cf2\b0 Opens a new window to view and modify all application-wide default settings stored in \cf3 `appsettings.json`\cf2 . This includes default paths, SMTP server details, default logging levels, operational parameters (like timeouts, financial year start), IPC settings, and the default AutoRun check hour. Changes saved here affect the application's default behavior for all users unless overridden by user-specific settings (e.g., custom email lists). \cf6\i Modifying these settings requires understanding their impact. Some changes may require an application restart.\cf2\i0\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf5\b\f0 Help:\cf2\b0  Displays this help information.\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\cf1\b\fs24 Automated Features\cf2\b0\fs20\par
\cf4\b\fs22 Auto-Run Feature:\cf2\b0\fs20\par
When the \cf5\b Enable Daily Auto Run @ \{\b {AUTO_RUN_HOUR}:00\b0\}\cf2\b0  button shows green (enabled), the application will automatically check around \b{AUTO_RUN_HOUR}:00\b0\cf2  each day to run any pending automated reports.\par
Automated reports are defined and managed via the \cf5\b Options -> Manage Automated Reports...\cf2\b0  window. In that window, you can add new report types, edit their properties (like schedule, template, email details), and enable or disable them individually.\par
The definitions for these automated reports are stored in a separate file named \cf3 `autoReportDefinitions.json`\cf2 , located in the same directory as `appsettings.json`.\par
Automated reports use email recipients and greetings configured for their specific 'Recipient Category Key' and 'Greeting Key' (see 'Manage Email Recipients' and 'Manage Email Greetings' forms, and default settings in `appsettings.json`). The status of the auto-run process is displayed in the right-hand side of the status bar.\par
The application keeps track of which reports have successfully run for the day in `appsettings.json` (under the `AutoRunProcess:DailyRunStatus` section) to avoid duplicate runs if the application is restarted.\par
\par
\cf4\b\fs22 Automated Archiving:\cf2\b0\fs20\par
The application performs automated archiving on start-up:\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Log Files:\b0  Log files older than the configured number of days (default {LOG_ARCHIVE_DAYS}, see \cf3 Logging:LogArchiveOlderThanDays\cf2  in `appsettings.json`) are moved to an 'Archive' subfolder.\par
    \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Report Files:\b0\par

\pard\fi-720\li1080       \f1\'b7\tab\i\f0  Final Reports:\i0  Previous calendar year folders are moved into a main archive folder (name configurable via \cf3 OperationalParameters:ReportArchiveFolderName\cf2 . Default: {REPORT_ARCHIVE_FOLDER_NAME})\par 
	\f1\'b7\tab\i\f0 Raw Reports:\i0  Files older than a configured number of days (default {RAW_REPORTS_ARCHIVE_DAYS}, see \cf3 OperationalParameters:ArchiveRawReportsOlderThanDays\cf2 ) are moved into an '\{REPORT_ARCHIVE_FOLDER_NAME\}\\YYYY-MM' subfolder within their respective report type directory.\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\cf1\b\fs24 Configuration Files Overview\cf2\b0\fs20\par
The application uses several configuration files:\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\cf3\b\f0 appsettings.json:\cf2\b0  The main configuration file. Stores application-wide defaults: critical paths, SMTP details, default email recipients/greetings, auto-run operational state (like `LastRunDate`, `DailyRunStatus`, `CheckHour` under `AutoRunProcess`), logging levels, and other operational parameters. Most of these can now be edited via the new \cf5\b Settings...\cf2\b0  menu. \cf6\i Modifying this file directly requires caution.\cf2\i0\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf3\b\f0 autoReportDefinitions.json:\cf2\b0  Located in the same directory as `appsettings.json`, this file stores the list of all automated report definitions. It is managed via the \cf5\b Options -> Manage Automated Reports...\cf2\b0  window.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 User-Specific JSON Files:\b0  Stored in your user profile's AppData directory (typically \cf3 %APPDATA%\\HarlowSolutions\\QuoteConversionReportAutomation\\\cf2 ). They allow for personal customisations:\par

\pard\fi-720\li1080       \f1\'b7\tab\cf3\f0 user_email_settings.json:\cf2  Custom email recipient lists (overrides app defaults).\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf3\f0 user_greeting_settings.json:\cf2  Custom email greetings (overrides app defaults).\par
      \f1\'b7\tab\cf3\f0 custom_bank_holidays.json:\cf2  Custom bank holidays.\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
\cf1\b\fs24 Troubleshooting\cf2\b0\fs20\par
If you encounter issues, consider the following steps:\par

\pard\fi-360\li720    \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 "Config Error" Status:\b0  Check essential file paths via \cf5\b Options -> View Configuration\cf2\b0  or edit them via \cf5\b Settings...\cf2\b0 . Ensure files/folders exist and are accessible.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Report Generation Fails:\b0  Ensure Crystal Report Wrapper service can run (check path in Settings), .rpt file path is correct, and check logs.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Excel Processing Fails:\b0  Check template paths/files (in Settings) and write permissions for output directories.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Email Sending Fails:\b0  Verify SMTP settings (in Settings) and network connectivity. Check recipient lists and greetings via their respective 'Manage...' options.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Auto-Run Not Working:\b0  Confirm main auto-run is enabled, individual reports are enabled and correctly configured (via \cf5\b Manage Automated Reports...\cf2\b0 ), and check the auto-run hour (in Settings). Review `appsettings.json` (`AutoRunProcess` section) and `autoReportDefinitions.json` if issues persist.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\cf6\b\f0 Check Application Logs:\cf2\b0  Always the best source for detailed errors. Access via \cf5\b Options -> Open Logs Folder\cf2\b0 .\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Incorrect Formulae in Excel:\b0  The application copies formulae from row 6 of the 'Analysis' sheet in the template. Ensure these are correct in your template files.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 User Settings Not Applying:\b0  Check the JSON files in your AppData folder mentioned under 'Configuration Files Overview'. Deleting a corrupted user settings file reverts that specific setting type to application defaults.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Manual Refresh Reports (Pivots/Slicers):\b0  For Monthly, Quarterly, Annual, Custom reports, carefully follow on-screen prompts to \b Enable Editing\b0 , \b Refresh Pivots/Slicers\b0  in Excel, \b Save\b0 , and \b Close\b0  before confirming in the app.\par
   \f1\'b7\tab\b\f0 Contact IT Dept:\b0  If problems persist, contact IT with details and relevant logs.\par

\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\par
Thank you for using the {APP_NAME} program!\par
